m2= 3.00 L=6: fitted c = -0.500000; max residual |a + c b| = 0.0

=> T_mn is an exactly (off-shell) conserved, symmetric, local stress; with
   S = S_FP(h) + S_m + kappa * c * sum h_mn T_mn and  delta h = nabla xi + nabla xi,
   delta phi = kappa L_xi phi, the coupled action is gauge invariant at O(kappa) EXACTLY.

== Killing restriction: pseudo-rotation  L_w phi = w_{nu mu} x_mu D_nu phi  (D = symmetric difference) ==
rotation in plane (0,1): max |delta S_m| = 0.0
rotation in plane (0,3): max |delta S_m| = 0.0
rotation in plane (2,3): max |delta S_m| = 0.0
=> the restriction of the matter gauge transformation to each lattice Killing rotation
   (including (4,j) 'Euclidean boosts') is an exact symmetry of the free lattice scalar.
